# CatDex — Product Design

## North star

Every session should make the player want **one more capture**. Design for delight at discovery, not admin forms.

## Core loop

```
Explore map → Spot / approach → Capture (camera) → Living analysis → Reward wow → CatDex + map pin
```

Secondary: missions / XP / badges reinforce return visits; never block the first capture behind heavy setup.

## Priorities (highest first)

1. **Capture pleasure** — celebrate before edit (`app/reward.tsx`, `src/components/reward/`)
2. **Narrative onboarding** — story beats, not SaaS slides (`app/(auth)/intro` → photo → permissions → reward)
3. **Lightweight signup** — multi-step, soft password UI
4. **Micro-interactions** — haptics/sounds gated by settings
5. **CatDex visual language** — halos, paws, rarity glow, filled icons

## Product rules

- Permissions (camera/location) are asked **in context** on the map / capture gate — not as a wall of screens before first value
- Welcome = full-bleed hero (map), brand-forward, short proof + CTAs — no heavy white sheet
- Community “mystery” cats stay mysterious until the player captures them
- Prefer one clear CTA per screen; avoid dashboard clutter on emotional moments

## Out of scope for MVP polish

- Social feed, chat, marketplace
- Hardcore MMO inventory systems
- Dark-mode-first redesign (product is white-first + indigo)

